    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0048" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg22"/>

                <head>*No. 4.<seg type="margin">[8]</seg></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Articles between the
                            United States of America and His Britannic Majesty</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1782-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 30, 1782</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> II.</p>
                <p>“From the northwest angle of Nova Scotia” * * * “through Lake Superior” * * * “to
                    the Long Lake; thence through the middle of said Long Lake, and the
                    water-communication between it and the Lake of the Woods, to the said Lake of
                    the Woods; thence through the said lake to the most northwestern point thereof,
                    and from thence on a due west course.” * * * * *<seg type="margin">First treaty
                        between the United States and Great Britain adopts for boundary a due west
                        course.</seg></p>
            </div>
